  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    # Find all coordinates where value is 5\n    coords = []\n    for i, row in enumerate(grid):\n        for j, val in enumerate(row):\n            if val == 5:\n                coords.append((i, j))\n    \n    if not coords:\n        return []\n    \n    min_row = min(r for r, c in coords)\n    max_row = max(r for r, c in coords)\n    min_col = min(c for r, c in coords)\n    max_col = max(c for r, c in coords)\n    \n    # Extract the subgrid: extend 1 row up and 1 row down from the 5s,\n    # keep the same column range\n    result = []\n    for r in range(min_row - 1, max_row + 2):\n        new_row = []\n        for c in range(min_col, max_col + 1):\n            new_row.append(grid[r][c])\n        result.append(new_row)\n    \n    return result\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    # Find all coordinates where value is 5\n    coords = []\n    for i, row in enumerate(grid):\n        for j, val in enumerate(row):\n            if val == 5:\n                coords.append((i, j))\n    \n    if not coords:\n        return []\n    \n    min_row = min(r for r, c in coords)\n    max_row = max(r for r, c in coords)\n    min_col = min(c for r, c in coords)\n    max_col = max(c for r, c in coords)\n    \n    # Extract the subgrid: extend 1 row up and 1 row down from the 5s,\n    # keep the same column range\n    result = []\n    for r in range(min_row - 1, max_row + 2):\n        new_row = []\n        for c in range(min_col, max_col + 1):\n            new_row.append(grid[r][c])\n        result.append(new_row)\n    \n    return result",
